Re-measure the canvas when the timeline appears, so clicks hit what they aim at.

CW and CH are read from the canvas in R.resize(), which runs at boot, on window
resize, and when the sidebar is toggled. rebuildAll() then reveals the timeline —
`$("timeline").style.display = "block"` — which shortens the canvas by the
timeline's height, and nothing re-measures. Since the timeline is shown whenever
there is data, every session runs with CW/CH describing a canvas taller than the
one on screen.

Two things break as a result. The renderer keeps drawing into the taller buffer
at the old camera aspect, so the map is drawn slightly stretched vertically and
the browser scales it down to fit. And pick() maps a click to normalised device
coordinates by dividing by the stale CH, so the ray goes somewhere other than
where the pointer is: measured at 1280x820, CH was 770 against a canvas 708 tall,
putting the ray about 79 world units off a node it was aimed dead centre at.
Clicking a conversation, hovering for its tooltip, and the label positions
computed by R.project() are all off by that margin.

It reads as "clicking nodes does nothing" rather than as a sizing bug, which is
probably why it survives: the offset is only about 9% of the height, so the map
still looks right and the labels look merely untidy.

Verified before and after at both desktop and phone viewports: CH now matches the
canvas height exactly, a ray aimed at a node's projected centre passes within a
fraction of a unit of it instead of 79, and tapping a node opens its conversation.

diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
index 184d2c6..7d7c140 100644
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -1831,6 +1831,9 @@ let searchBlobs = [];
 async function rebuildAll(fresh){
   $("empty").style.display = S.convs.length ? "none" : "flex";
   $("timeline").style.display = S.convs.length ? "block" : "none";
+  // Showing the timeline shortens the canvas, and CW/CH plus the camera aspect
+  // have to follow it — picking and label placement both divide by them.
+  R.resize();
   if (!S.convs.length){ S.nodes = []; S.edges = []; G.N = 0; if (R.points) R.points.visible = false; if (R.lines) R.lines.visible = false; G.needsRender = true; updateCounts(); return; }
   toast(`Linking ${S.convs.length.toLocaleString()} conversations by meaning…`, { sticky: true });
   await yieldUI();
